    "body":  "## Observed failure\n\nAfter PR #294 merged, a fresh real Chromium Pages acceptance reproduced an Example replacement failure on current-main-derived PR #287 head `a5c749b066b2acf3939ebc6b7131b8407901048b`.\n\nWorkflow: [Pages Chromium #45788420150](https://github.com/odango-chan/ca-skill-studio-demo/actions/runs/45788420150), job `build`, step `Real Chromium acceptance at the default Pages root`.\n\nThe failure occurs at `publish-dependency-lock` while checking the optional workspace settings file:\n\n`Unable to read file \u0027.vscode/settings.json\u0027 (EntryNotFound / ENOENT)`.\n\nThe transaction correctly rolls back and restores the previous Example; it does not corrupt the workspace. However, the explicit replacement does not complete.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`experiments/ide-host/vscode/src/sample-loader.mjs` → `persistExampleDependenciesIfAbsent()` defines a local `exists()` helper that treats only `error.code === \"FileNotFound\"` as absence.\n\nThe transaction helpers added by #294 already recognize `FileNotFound`, `EntryNotFound` and ENOENT, but this optional `.vscode/settings.json` existence check does not. Theia Browser-only OPFS can report a missing optional settings file as `EntryNotFound`, so the missing file is incorrectly escalated as a fatal import error.\n\nThis is a distinct uncovered call site from #294\u0027s stale `.skill-studio/dependencies` directory-entry handling. Do not weaken normal Skill source or transaction-manifest missing-file checks.\n\n## Required change\n\n1. Reuse a narrowly scoped missing-entry predicate for the optional settings existence check (`FileNotFound`, `EntryNotFound`, ENOENT); propagate permission, I/O and other unexpected errors.\n2. Add a deterministic regression that seeds an existing Example, performs confirmed replacement, and makes `stat()` report `EntryNotFound` for the missing candidate `.vscode/settings.json`.\n3. Assert replacement commits, the current dependency lock is written, the previous Example is not restored, and the workspace is READY.\n4. Keep failure-atomic rollback and existing stale dependency-cache tests intact.\n5. Re-run exact-head PR Verify, Native Windows, IDE Host, Browser Host, Browser-Only Chromium and Pages Chromium after the fix. A clean retry without a code fix is not resolution.\n\n## Relations\n\n- Parent: #279 (Product Acceptance / architecture audit).\n- Related: #280 (Example replacement failure atomicity), fixed by #294 but this OPFS settings-file variant remained uncovered.\n- Reproduced by Pages Chromium on #287; do not attribute the failure to the Welcome copy change.",
